  "final_message": "`OrderPlaced` now has `amountCents` and `createdAt`, but I didn't do it as a plain rename. `billing-service` and `analytics-ingest` read this event, and the project rules (ARCH-4) say renames must go through deprecation, so a straight rename would have broken both. Instead, the event now carries both sets of names:\n\n- **New fields:** `createdAt` and `amountCents`.\n- **Old fields still sent:** `placedAt` and `totalCents` carry the same values and are marked `@deprecated` in `src/core/events.ts`, so consumers still compile and run.\n- **`schemaVersion` stays at 3**, since this only adds fields.\n- **Tests:** they now check both the new and old fields. All 39 pass and the dependency checks are clean.\n\nI left the HTTP responses alone (`POST /orders`, `GET /orders/{id}` still return `placedAt`/`totalCents`). You asked only about the event, and web-storefront depends on those responses staying backward compatible (ARCH-8).\n\n**To finish the rename:**\n1. Tell the billing and analytics teams to switch to `amountCents` and `createdAt`.\n2. Once both have deployed, remove `placedAt` and `totalCents` from the event and bump `schemaVersion` to 4, since removing fields breaks older readers.\n\nNothing is committed yet. Should I commit it on a branch and open a PR?",
